data: {"level":2,"reviewed":{"level":2,"label":"formula / approach","text":"Unstratified: the test count is `ceil(test_size * n)`, and one `rng.permutation(n)` gives the rows.\nStratified: compute `test_size * n_j` for each class, floor it, then give the leftover test rows\nto the classes with the largest fractional parts, breaking ties by the earlier class. Then draw one\npermutation per class, in ascending class order."},"hints_note":null}

